Amendment to Task 1.2: move AsyncAPI example into examples/, add enum-validated status field

Summary: Moved ExampleAsyncApiChannels.scala/ExampleEvent from src/main/scala/$package$/
to src/main/scala/$package$/examples/ (package $package$.examples) - the plugin's
asyncApiChannelsClass setting updated to match. Renamed and moved the test file
from ExampleAsyncApiChannelsSuite.scala to examples/AsyncApiChannelsExampleSuite.scala,
adopting ClientResilienceExampleSuite's own <Concept>ExampleSuite naming convention.
Added a status: String field to ExampleEvent, constrained via
Validator.enumeration(List("created","updated","deleted")).encode(identity) +
Schema.derived[...].modify(_.status)(_.validate(...)) - same pattern order-service's
OrderStatusChangedEvent uses - so the generated AsyncAPI docs visibly show an enum
constraint, not just flat scalar fields.

Files changed:
- src/main/g8/build.sbt (asyncApiChannelsClass path update)
- src/main/g8/src/main/scala/$package$/examples/ExampleAsyncApiChannels.scala (moved + enum field)
- src/main/g8/src/test/scala/$package$/examples/AsyncApiChannelsExampleSuite.scala (moved, renamed, +1 test)

Why: User feedback mid-task - the AsyncAPI example should live alongside the httpclient
example in examples/ for discoverability/consistency, and the enum field makes the
generated docs demonstrably richer than a trivial example.

